  "_throughput_scale_note": "Model throughput figures are for the reference machine of each kind: c7i.2xlarge (8 vCPU) for cpu, one L40S (g6e.xlarge) for gpu. throughput_scale multiplies them: CPU by vCPU count (older Ice Lake 0.85), GPU by GPU count (p5: 8 H100 at about 2x an L40S each). Assumptions except c7i.2xlarge, which was measured. c7a (AMD Genoa) measured 7.9 tok/s decode on c7a.xlarge on 2026-11-16, so its scale is 1.2 per 4 vCPU. r-family 4xlarge (16 vCPU): Intel measured 3.5 tok/s at 4 vCPU vs AMD 7.9, so Intel 4xlarge is scaled ~1.0 and AMD ~2.4; assumptions until measured. Spot prices for r-family are the higher of us-east-1a/1b on 2026-11-17."
